CVE-2025-0108
--------------------
Web request to the management interface is handled by three separate components: Nginx, Apache, and the PHP application itself.

Authentication is set at the Nginx level and based on HTTP headers, which we can set almost arbitrarily. Our request is then re-processed again in Apache, which may process the path or
headers differently to Nginx! Then and only then is the request handed down to PHP.

